            <ArticleTitle>Response to Cabazitaxel Beyond 20 Cycles in A Patient with Penile Metastasis of Prostate Cancer: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2985-2988</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Penile metastases are extremely rare events and generally occurs at a late stage of primary disease. They mostlyoriginate from prostate and bladder in the genitourinary tract. Penile metastases have a dismal prognosis and verylow survival rates. We report a case of penile metastasis in 70-year-old geriatric male patient with prostatic adenocarcinomawho was treated with cabazitaxel chemotherapy beyond 20 cycles with a good response and acceptableminimal toxicity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
